    Bound held-charge history and verify full overrun-floor distinction
    
    T18 verifies that a held charge equal to its cap may be released down to a
    positively verified same-session terminal reading; T19 verifies that a charge
    above its cap is retained in full through both manual resolution and reconcile
    (tokens, CPU and wall independently). T20 verifies repeated reconciliation does
    not append history once the charge floor is stable.
    
    Engine rule was already committed in 48f8c50c; this change adds only the
    missing focused regression and audit note. No live ledger, permits or dispatch.

