+
+## Final focused charge-floor review
+
+Recovery-steward commit `48f8c50c` already implemented the reviewed rule: a
+held charge above its cap is observed debt and is retained in full, while a
+charge equal to the cap is only reserved liability and may be released by a
+positively verified same-session terminal measurement. `retain_overrun_floor`
+applies the rule independently to tokens/CPU/wall in both `finalize_locked` and
+`resolve_locked`. T18 (charge == cap, terminal reading 120 of 1000) verifies the
+lawful release; T19 (cap 100, charge 150, stale terminal reading 90) verifies
+the full 150 is retained through both manual resolution and reconcile. T20
+verifies repeated reconciliation stops appending history once the floor is
+stable. Against parent `48f8c50c^`, T13, T18 and T19 fail; all 20 cases pass at
+HEAD.
